##  Getting Started

### Prerequisites

```bash
# Required
- Python 3.10+ (I use 3.11)
- PostgreSQL 14+ (I use 18)

# AI API Keys (at least one)
- Groq API (free, recommended): https://console.groq.com
- Google Gemini (free): https://makersuite.google.com
- OpenAI (optional): https://platform.openai.com
```

### Quick Setup

```bash
# 1. Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/MissBittu/my_buddy--agentic-ai-based-persanal-assistant-.git
cd cosmic-assistant/backend

# 2. Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# 3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Setup PostgreSQL
createdb cosmic_assistant  # or use pgAdmin

# 5. Configure environment
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env - add your database credentials and API keys

# 6. Initialize database
python setup_postgres.py

# 7. Run server
python main.py
```

### Test AI Features

```bash
# Visit interactive API docs
http://localhost:8000/api/docs

# Or use curl
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/auth/signup \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"test@example.com","password":"Test123!","full_name":"Test User"}'

# Get your token from response, then:
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/ai/analyze-task \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"task_title":"Build authentication system","task_description":"JWT-based auth with refresh tokens"}'
```

